{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"next-batch rebuilt on one slim pass (commit 451212e377a, branch fix-nb-lean-pass, make verify running). Cause of the per-call cost: compute() reduced every ticket in full, then list_states reduced the whole store again, both alive at once. Measured on a clone of the live store (5,769 tickets): one call's traced peak 517 MB -> 64 MB; 9 concurrent calls on threads 3,991 MB -> 684 MB process RSS (macOS). Output identical to the old code for all 11 open epics. Linux re-measurement in the server image is running; a 4-at-a-time queue gets added only if the burst still approaches the 3.63 GiB limit. Other whole-store reads (list, search, deps, validate) are not changed by this commit."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793292630610962001,"uuid":"4960ce88-dc9c-4900-81a4-73fceccc816f"}